sentences.l:
For I myself will remain in the gathering-place of the ships,
but a companion I am sending among the many Myrmidons
to fight;

in all of them the heart was stirred up, and the battle-lines were moved,
hoping that beside the ships the fleet-footed son of Peleus
had cast off his wrath and chosen friendship;

and he, on his back, in the dust
fell down, wailing, and his companions were thrown into panic about him,
the Paeonians;
